    "id": "thorn-philosophy",
    "name": "Thorn Philosophy",
    "category": "Customs",
    "body": "Thorn philosophy holds that worth is revealed through what endures. Loyalty matters more after testing, courage matters when fear is justified, and promises matter when keeping them costs something. Strength also creates responsibility: rulers are expected to protect what has placed itself in their care. Thorn culture does not glorify pointless pain; needless cruelty that damages one's own people is treated as failure, not strength.",
